Fillets: a rounding's end at a vertex where a sliver lies between the
blend's faces and the face beyond the edge its contact left its face by:
that face's OnSame end across the sliver, which is consumed (mitcad#343).

The case: a wall's foot on a floor is rounded with 0.5, the radius of an
earlier rounding round the foot of the wall's end (a B-spline between the
floor and a torus that is tangent to the wall along a circle). At both
ends of the foot the contact on the wall leaves the wall across the wall's
edge with that earlier rounding, where its ball is the new one's, before
the end of the foot edge. At one end the foot edge runs into that
rounding's floor contact at the vertex: port patch 0540 builds that OnSame
end, the earlier rounding growing up to the section they share. At the
other end a step's end face is left between the floor, the wall and the
earlier rounding: a triangle 0.16 by 0.02 (the wall narrowing to an edge
0.02 long). The vertex there has the floor, the wall and that sliver, all
three edges concave (AllSame); the corner found no face holding both
contacts' ends, walked round the vertex (PerformIntersectionAtEnd), and
the result had the blend running on to the floor's rim and was invalid
(a change of volume of 9.1 mm3 against the stored 0.70).

- ChFi3d_SliverFaceAtEnd: at a single stripe's end vertex of three faces,
  the blend's two and a face Fs whose vertices lie within the rounding's
  radius of each other, where one contact left its face across an edge
  Arcpiv not at the vertex (any edge of that face at the contact's end
  where that end is a vertex) whose face beyond, Fv, closes Fs: Fs's edges
  are its edge with each blend face at the vertex and edges with Fv, the
  edge with the contact's face running to a vertex of Arcpiv and the edge
  with the opposite face to a vertex Vprol of an edge Arcprol of Fv and
  the opposite face.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner: such an end is taken as Fv's OnSame
  end: the face at the end is Fv, the prolonged edge Arcprol from Vprol
  (where the OnSame end prolongs the edge at the vertex), the contact's
  point at a vertex put on Arcpiv, and Fs consumed (its edges cut at their
  vertices so that the builder drops it with them, as for a face consumed
  at an end along an edge). The rest is the OnSame end as before (0540's
  section in the tube of Fv).

On the stored body before the item the result is valid, with the stored
body's 193 faces and a change of volume of 0.70767 mm3 against the stored
0.70662; the earlier rounding grows at both ends as there. Other ends are
unchanged.

Upstream: new.
